<title>POLAND: Polish net forex reserves up to $21.5 bln May 1-20.</title>
<headline>Polish net forex reserves up to $21.5 bln May 1-20.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish net foreign currency reserves grew by $426 million in May 1-20 to $21.498 billion, the National Bank of Poland said.</p>
<p>It said net reserves fell $168 million in the January-May 20 period. </p>
<p>    POLISH RESERVES (bln dollars)  MAY 20     APRIL     MAY   96</p>
<p>    Official reserves	     21.498     21.072	22.010</p>
<p>    Net reserves			 na	   na	 18.014</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures in billions of dollars. Official reserves are those held by the state. Net reserves mean the total amount of hard currencies in the whole banking system.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
